          "note_id": "F2UGOUpcnlr",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "This paper presents Contrastive Video Textures for video synthesis by resampling frames from an input video. The model is video-specific and represents a video as a graph where nodes indicate individual frames and edges are transition probabilities. An output video is generated by traversing edges with high transition probabilities. A deep video interpolation model is used to make visual smoothness for large transitions. This model can be extended to an audio conditioned video synthesis task. ",
